# Site-specific PII patterns for the pre-commit guard.
#
#   cp .githooks/pii-patterns.example .githooks/pii-patterns
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE and is tracked. The copy you create is gitignored,
# because a guard that lists your real domain, IP, phone numbers and email
# addresses is itself a published copy of all of them.
#
# One extended-regex per line. '#' starts a comment.

# Your production host and its address
# your-domain\.example
# 203\.0\.113\.10

# Email domains that should never appear in a commit
# @your-domain\.example
# @your-personal-domain\.example

# Phone numbers, tolerant of separators
# \b555[ .-]*0100[ .-]*0000\b
